The whole architecture, one model, one stage at a time — run it and read.

model: examples/walkthrough.yaml

[1] YAML text -> validated Spec  (math_spec.to_spec)
    dimensions   snapshot, generator
    parameters   p_max, load, cost
    variables    p
    constraints  power_balance
    expressions  total_supply    <- tier 2, still present
    macros       weighted_sum   <- tier 2, still present

[2] expand macros / named expressions -> core AST  (math_spec.to_program)
    written      'sum(weighted_sum(p, cost, over=generator))'
    core AST     Sum(operand=Sum(operand=Multiply(left=Variable(name='p'), right=Parameter(name='cost')), over=('generator',)), over=('snapshot',))
                 ^ the macro is gone: sum(p * cost, over=generator)

[3] a spec -> the program both lanes build from  (math_spec.to_program)
    Program(
      VariableDeclaration(name='p', dims=('snapshot', 'generator'), where=ParameterComparisonNode(name='p_max', op='>', value=0.0), lower=Constant(value=0.0), upper=Parameter(name='p_max'), variable_type='continuous', absence='undefined')
      ConstraintDeclaration(name='power_balance', dims=('snapshot',), lhs=Sum(operand=Variable(name='p'), over=('generator',)), sense='==', rhs=Parameter(name='load'), where=None)
      ObjectiveDeclaration(sense='minimize', expression=Sum(operand=Sum(operand=Multiply(left=Variable(name='p'), right=Parameter(name='cost')), over=('generator',)), over=('snapshot',)))
    )
    ^ frozen dataclasses, no macro, no YAML, no linopy, no engine

[4] plan + data -> the model frames  (relational/engines/polars/engine.py)
    cols                   18 rows
    obj                     6 rows
    rows                    6 rows
    A                      18 rows

    cols/rows/A/obj = the LP itself, in COO form:
    a column is a bound and a cost, a row a sense and a rhs,
    and A is every nonzero coefficient as (row, col, coeff).

    where "p_max > 0" is not a mask array — it is row absence:
    p has 18 rows, not 24: retired oil never becomes a column.
    shape: (4, 3)
    ┌──────────┬───────────┬───────────┐
    │ snapshot ┆ generator ┆ var_label │
    │ ---      ┆ ---       ┆ ---       │
    │ i64      ┆ enum      ┆ i64       │
    ╞══════════╪═══════════╪═══════════╡
    │ 0        ┆ wind      ┆ 0         │
    │ 0        ┆ solar     ┆ 1         │
    │ 0        ┆ gas       ┆ 2         │
    │ 1        ┆ wind      ┆ 3         │
    └──────────┴───────────┴───────────┘

[5] sink: stream the frames to an LP file  (relational/sinks/writers/lp_file.py)
    min
    
    obj:
    +50.0 x2
    +50.0 x5
    +50.0 x8
    +50.0 x11
    +50.0 x14
    +50.0 x17
    
    s.t.
    ... (64 lines total)

[6] sink: batches -> highspy -> solution frames  (relational/sinks/solvers/highs.py)
    status     ok (optimal)
    objective  1,000.0
    shape: (6, 3)
    ┌──────────┬───────────┬───────┐
    │ snapshot ┆ generator ┆ value │
    │ ---      ┆ ---       ┆ ---   │
    │ i64      ┆ str       ┆ f64   │
    ╞══════════╪═══════════╪═══════╡
    │ 0        ┆ wind      ┆ 80.0  │
    │ 0        ┆ solar     ┆ 0.0   │
    │ 0        ┆ gas       ┆ 0.0   │
    │ 1        ┆ wind      ┆ 60.0  │
    │ 1        ┆ solar     ┆ 60.0  │
    │ 1        ┆ gas       ┆ 0.0   │
    └──────────┴───────────┴───────┘
    shape: (3, 2)
    ┌──────────┬───────┐
    │ snapshot ┆ value │
    │ ---      ┆ ---   │
    │ i64      ┆ f64   │
    ╞══════════╪═══════╡
    │ 0        ┆ 80.0  │
    │ 1        ┆ 120.0 │
    │ 2        ┆ 150.0 │
    └──────────┴───────┘
                 ^ the named expression, read back at the solution

[7] and what the language refuses  (math_spec)

    an operator that is not in the closed built-in set:
    caught by check() as SchemaError
      Constraint 'cumulative': Unknown operator 'cumsum'.
      Available: ['at', 'shift', 'sum', 'sum_back']
      Define 'cumsum' as a macro under 'macros:' if it composes built-ins; if the math is not sayable in the language, use a declared escape.

    variable x variable x variable — the ceiling is degree 2, not "nonlinear is fine":
    caught by check() as SchemaError
      The objective: this product is degree 3. The language takes degree 2 and nothing above it.
      Multiply by a parameter instead, or give the inner product a name — a variable constrained to equal it is degree 1 wherever it is used.

docs/about/architecture.md has the rules these stages enforce.
